{title: Perfumer of the Wall}
{subtitle: Nehemiah 3:30; 3:1–30; 4:1–6; 6:15–16}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Bb] [Dm7] |
| [Ebmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Next to Uz[Bb]ziel [Dm7]the goldsmith stood [Ebmaj7]
A per[Bb]fumer [Dm7]with hands that could [Ebmaj7]build
In the [Gm7]city of Jeru[F]salem
They worked [Ebmaj7]side by side
Re[Bb]stored the [Dm7]stone as far as the Broad [Ebmaj7]Wall
[Gm7]No one asked for [F]glory or [Ebmaj7]fame
Just [Gm7]the task at [F]hand in the [Ebmaj7]dust
Shoulder to shoul[Fsus4]der in the [F]rain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Hana[Bb]niah son of Uz[Dm7]ziel
Building the wall [Ebmaj7]with steady hand
[Bb]Next to him a perfu[Dm7]mer stood
[Ebmaj7]Adding their part to the plan
The [Gm7]gaps were [F]closed the work [Ebmaj7]went on
[Cm7]Under the eyes [F7sus4]of the [Bb]Lord [Dm7][Ebmaj7]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Sanbal[Bb]lat and [Dm7]Tobiah grew fu[Ebmaj7]rious
Seeing the [Bb]gaps [Dm7]being [Ebmaj7]closed
They [Bb]conspired to fight [Dm7]against Jerusa[Ebmaj7]lem
To [Bb]throw it into [Dm7]confusion and [Ebmaj7]loss
But [Gm7]we prayed to our [F]God day and [Ebmaj7]night
Posting [Gm7]guards against [F]their threat [Ebmaj7]
The [Gm7]laborers said the [F]strength was fail[Ebmaj7]ing
Too much [F]rubble on the street
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Hana[Bb]niah son of Uz[Dm7]ziel
Building the wall [Ebmaj7]with steady hand
[Bb]Next to him a perfu[Dm7]mer stood
[Ebmaj7]Adding their part to the plan
The [Gm7]gaps were [F]closed the work [Ebmaj7]went on
[Cm7]Under the eyes [F7]of the [Bb]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ebmaj7]Enemies whispered we would be killed
Be[Gm7]fore they saw the stone set
But the [Ebmaj7]Jews warned us ten times over
We [Gm7]did not let our spirits get wet
The [Ebmaj7]nations around were af[Gm7]raid
When the [Cm7]wall was finally [F7sus4]done
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Fif-ty-two days the [Dm7]work was finished [Ebmaj7]
The [Bb]enemies confidence [Dm7]was gone
[Ebmaj7]The wall stands firm in the history
[Cm7]A [F7]testament to [Bb]the strong
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
